> This document provides an overview of the comprehensive benefits package offered to eligible employees at NexaTech Solutions Inc. We are proud to invest in the health, well-being, and financial security of our employees and their families.

## 1. Introduction

At NexaTech, we understand that our employees are our most valuable asset. Our benefits program is designed to be comprehensive, competitive, and flexible to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. This document provides a summary of the key benefits available to you. For full details, please refer to the official plan documents.

## 2. Health and Wellness

### 2.1. Medical Insurance

We offer a choice of medical plans through a national carrier, including PPO and HDHP options. The company pays a significant portion of the premium for employees and their dependents.

### 2.2. Dental Insurance

Our dental plan covers preventive, basic, and major restorative services.

### 2.3. Vision Insurance

Our vision plan provides coverage for eye exams, glasses, and contact lenses.

### 2.4. Employee Assistance Program (EAP)

The EAP provides confidential, 24/7 support for a wide range of personal and work-related issues, including stress, financial concerns, and mental health. This service is provided at no cost to employees.

## 3. Financial Security

### 3.1. 401(k) Retirement Savings Plan

We offer a 401(k) plan to help you save for retirement. The company matches 100% of your contributions up to 4% of your eligible compensation.

### 3.2. Life and Disability Insurance

*   **Life Insurance:** The company provides basic life insurance coverage at no cost to you.
*   **Short-Term Disability (STD):** STD insurance provides income replacement if you are unable to work due to a non-work-related illness or injury.
*   **Long-Term Disability (LTD):** LTD insurance provides continued income replacement for extended periods of disability.

## 4. Time Off

### 4.1. Flexible Paid Time Off (PTO)

We offer a flexible PTO policy for vacation and personal time. We encourage employees to take at least 20 days off per year to rest and recharge.

### 4.2. Sick Leave

We provide paid sick leave for when you are unable to work due to illness or to care for a sick family member.

### 4.3. Company Holidays

We observe 11 paid company holidays each year.

## 5. Professional Development

### 5.1. Professional Development Stipend

We provide an annual stipend of $2,000 for each employee to use for professional development opportunities, such as conferences, courses, and certifications.

### 5.2. Online Learning

We provide access to a variety of online learning platforms with thousands of courses on a wide range of topics.

